                <pb facs="0365" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg291"/>


                <head>Mr. Webb to Mr. Washburn.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rio de Janeiro,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 26, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    instructions have been issued by the Brazilian government to their
                    representatives in the river Plate and its vicinity withdrawing all obstructions
                    to your passing to your post of duty whenever it shall be your pleasure to
                    repair thereto.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. WATSON WEBB</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles A. Washburn,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister Resident to
                        Paraguay.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
